甚至可能在虐待他。

500
00:21:34.340 --> 00:21:41.800
So he starts offering Jim a bunch of unsolicited advice, which backfires when Jim pranks him
于是他开始给吉姆提供一堆不请自来的建议，结果却弄巧成拙，遭到吉姆的恶作剧整蛊

501
00:21:41.800 --> 00:21:46.300
into confiding that things are terrible between him and Pam.
吐露他和帕姆之间的关系糟糕透顶。

502
00:21:46.520 --> 00:21:47.820
It starts this whole runner.
这就开启了整条故事线。

503
00:21:48.060 --> 00:21:48.380
Yeah.
对。

504
00:21:48.380 --> 00:21:56.260
But this episode begins with a very famous cold open, the Cheese Puff Cold Open.
但这一集是从一个非常著名的冷开场开始的，也就是起司球冷开场。

505
00:21:56.260 --> 00:21:57.000
It is.
确实如此。

506
00:21:57.160 --> 00:21:58.900
I titled it the Cheese Puff.
我给它起名叫起司球。

507
00:21:59.640 --> 00:22:02.060
I loved doing this cold open so much.
我太喜欢拍这个冷开场了。

508
00:22:02.060 --> 00:22:03.780
I have so many questions for you.
我有好多问题想问你。

509
00:22:03.940 --> 00:22:05.200
I have so many questions.
我有好多问题。

510
00:22:05.600 --> 00:22:06.700
Should we describe it?
我们要不要描述一下？

511
00:22:07.040 --> 00:22:07.780
Describe it.
描述一下吧。

512
00:22:08.280 --> 00:22:08.640
All right.
好的。

513
00:22:09.560 --> 00:22:17.540
It's Pam, Michael, and Ryan tossing Cheese Puffs into one another's mouths in various ways.
画面里是帕姆、迈克尔和瑞恩用各种方式把起司球扔进彼此嘴里。

514
00:22:17.920 --> 00:22:18.120
Right.
没错。

515
00:22:18.220 --> 00:22:22.440
It's like the things you see on like YouTube of where the guy bounces the basketball off
就像你在油管上看到的那些视频，有个家伙把篮球弹到

516
00:22:22.440 --> 00:22:25.820
like the back of a wall and it hits the other side of the wall and it goes in the hoop.
墙的背面，然后篮球弹到墙的另一侧，空心入网。

517
00:22:26.200 --> 00:22:27.260
That's what you guys are doing.
这就是你们在做的事。

518
00:22:27.260 --> 00:22:28.940
But you're doing it with Cheese Puffs.
只不过你们用的是起司球。

519
00:22:28.940 --> 00:22:34.520
And I love the callback because, remember, this is what Michael took when he ran out
我特别喜欢这个呼应，因为大家还记得吧，这就是迈克尔在最后一天跑出

520
00:22:34.520 --> 00:22:36.360
of Dunder Mifflin on that last day.
邓德米弗林时拿走的东西。

521
00:22:36.560 --> 00:22:37.760
You have questions.
你有问题要问。

522
00:22:38.160 --> 00:22:40.640
We got a fan mail flurry about this.
我们收到了大量关于这个的粉丝来信。

523
00:22:41.180 --> 00:22:48.060
So first we reached out to writer Ryan Coe to find out like what was the inspiration for
所以首先我们联系了编剧瑞恩·科，想了解一下这个冷开场的灵感

524
00:22:48.060 --> 00:22:48.820
this cold open.
来源是什么。

525
00:22:48.980 --> 00:22:51.040
His response was so funny.
他的回复太搞笑了。

526
00:22:51.180 --> 00:22:51.780
It's so good.
太棒了。

527
00:22:51.780 --> 00:22:54.060
I actually spit out my coffee while listening to it.
我听的时候差点把咖啡喷出来。

528
00:22:54.140 --> 00:22:55.100
Yeah, we got to play it.
对，我们得放出来听听。

529
00:22:55.860 --> 00:22:56.260
Hi, Jenna.
嗨，珍娜。

530
00:22:56.460 --> 00:22:56.900
Hi, Angela.
嗨，安吉拉。

531
00:22:57.620 --> 00:22:59.280
Thanks for letting me talk about my episode.
谢谢你们让我聊聊我写的这一集。

532
00:22:59.660 --> 00:23:04.440
Jenna, you had mentioned that you love shooting that cold open with the cheese balls and you
珍娜，你曾提到你很喜欢和起司球一起拍摄那个冷开场，并且

533
00:23:04.440 --> 00:23:05.600
were wondering where it came from.
你想知道它的灵感是从哪来的。

534
00:23:05.880 --> 00:23:09.660
I remember that it was most of all a product of exhaustion.
我记得这主要是精疲力竭的产物。

535
00:23:09.880 --> 00:23:10.800
I'll back up a bit.
我倒回前面一点说。

536
00:23:11.480 --> 00:23:11.620
Yeah.
对。

537
00:23:11.860 --> 00:23:16.640
You know, for the first draft of my episode, I had written a cold open about how Ryan thought
你知道的，在我这一集的初稿里，我写了一个冷开场，讲的是瑞恩觉得

538
00:23:16.640 --> 00:23:19.420
Pam had a crush on him and no one liked it.
帕姆对有好感，但大家都不喜欢这个情节。

539
00:23:19.560 --> 00:23:21.600
So it was tossed out and we needed a new cold open.
所以它被废弃了，我们需要一个新的冷开场。

540
00:23:22.160 --> 00:23:25.180
And at this point in the season, all the writers were really exhausted.
而且在这个赛季的这个阶段，所有的编剧都真的筋疲力尽了。

541
00:23:25.480 --> 00:23:33.440
In season five, as you recall, we did 28 episodes and they were shot in a 10 consecutive weeks
正如你们所记得的，在第五季中，我们拍了28集，它们是在连续10周的

542
00:23:33.440 --> 00:23:38.520
of production, then a break so Steve could do a movie and then 18 straight weeks of production.
制作后休息一下，好让史蒂夫去拍电影，接着又是连续18周的制作。

543
00:23:39.060 --> 00:23:43.220
Other shows I've been on, I've told them that there was a stretch of 18 straight weeks
我在其他剧组工作时，曾告诉过他们我们曾经连续18周进行

544
00:23:43.220 --> 00:23:45.900
of production and they do not believe we did that.
制作，他们根本不相信我们做过这种事。

545
00:23:46.060 --> 00:23:51.180
In sort of sitcoms, it's more common to do two or three weeks on of production.
在情景喜剧里，通常的做法是连续制作两到三周。

546
00:23:51.780 --> 00:23:56.940
And then one week off so that the actors can recover and so the writers can catch up and
然后休息一周，以便演员们恢复体力，编剧们也能赶上进度

547
00:23:56.940 --> 00:23:58.080
don't get totally burned out.
不至于彻底精疲力竭。

548
00:23:58.460 --> 00:24:01.120
And so 18 straight weeks is a total death march.
所以连续18周简直就是一场死亡行军。

549
00:24:01.620 --> 00:24:06.000
And I remember at that time, a writer was going to go down and check out what was going
我记得当时，有个编剧准备下楼去看看片场到底

550
00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:06.780
down on set.
发生了什么。

551
00:24:07.440 --> 00:24:09.880
Paul or someone was like, do not go down there.
保罗或者谁当时说，千万别去那边。

552
00:24:09.880 --> 00:24:12.240
The actors are tired and are acting like huge ass.
演员们都很累，而且表现得像个混蛋。

553
00:24:12.560 --> 00:24:15.640
So, yeah, I remember it was a sort of rough time.
所以，是的，我记得那是一段挺艰难的时期。

554
00:24:15.940 --> 00:24:20.360
And so for the last half of season five, we were always behind.
所以在第五季的后半段，我们的进度一直落后。

555
00:24:20.760 --> 00:24:24.920
And I feel like we were working 11 or more hours pretty much every single day.
我觉得我们基本上每天都要工作11个小时甚至更久。

556
00:24:25.260 --> 00:24:30.580
I remember Mindy was really mad that it meant she had no social life and said something
我记得明迪非常生气，因为这意味着她没有社交生活了，还说了句

557
00:24:30.580 --> 00:24:32.960
like, I'm going to die alone because of this damn show.
类似于，我因为这个该死的节目要孤独终老了。

558
00:24:33.400 --> 00:24:38.920
So anyway, we were all very spent and we were trying to come up with a new cold open and
总之，我们当时都筋疲力尽，正试图想一个新的冷场白（片头前小品），

559
00:24:38.920 --> 00:24:40.940
it was either Aaron Schur or Paul.
要么是亚伦·舒尔，要么是保罗。

560
00:24:41.240 --> 00:24:45.060
They were both the guys that were really good at making something out of nothing.
他们俩都是那种特别擅长无中生有的人。

561
00:24:45.380 --> 00:24:50.300
And one of them said, I don't know, they're throwing cheese balls at each other.
其中一个人说，不知道，他们正把起司球扔向彼此呢。

562
00:24:50.680 --> 00:24:51.820
And everyone's like, great.
然后大家就说，太好了。

563
00:24:52.020 --> 00:24:52.840
We don't have to write anything.
我们什么都不用写了。

564
00:24:52.960 --> 00:24:53.320
That's awesome.
太棒了。

565
00:24:53.460 --> 00:24:53.600
Okay.
好的。

566
00:24:53.660 --> 00:24:54.880
That's the cold open cheese balls.
冷场白就是扔起司球了。

567
00:24:55.040 --> 00:24:55.240
All right.
行吧。

568
00:24:55.340 --> 00:24:55.680
Next.
下一个。

569
00:24:55.680 --> 00:25:00.580
As far as anything else about writing the episode, it was a long time ago and I don't
至于关于写这一集的其他事情，那是很久以前的事了，我

570
00:25:00.580 --> 00:25:03.140
really remember because I was tired.
记不太清，因为我太累了。

571
00:25:05.800 --> 00:25:07.680
Ryan, that made our day.
瑞恩，那可让我们高兴了一整天。

572
00:25:08.940 --> 00:25:16.260
I mean, look at this amazing piece of comedy that came out of just everyone being so tired.
我是说，看看这个精彩的喜剧片段，竟然源于大家当时都那么累。

573
00:25:16.580 --> 00:25:16.860
Fatigue.
疲惫。

574
00:25:17.160 --> 00:25:17.600
Yes.
是的。

575
00:25:18.060 --> 00:25:24.840
You guys might remember Ryan is our writer who wiped out while running past the speed reader
大家可能还记得，瑞恩就是我们那个在跑过测速雷达

576
00:25:24.840 --> 00:25:25.260
sign.
标志时摔倒的编剧。

577
00:25:25.260 --> 00:25:25.820
Yes.
是的。

578
00:25:26.260 --> 00:25:31.060
So Ryan, thank you so much for sharing your memory with us of the cheese ball cold open.
所以瑞恩，非常感谢你跟我们分享关于起司球冷场白的记忆。

579
00:25:31.260 --> 00:25:31.640
And now.
现在。

580
00:25:31.760 --> 00:25:34.160
And sorry if we were assholes that week.
如果那一周我们太混蛋的话，在此道歉。

581
00:25:34.740 --> 00:25:35.160
Yeah.
对啊。

582
00:25:35.280 --> 00:25:35.500
Sorry.
抱歉。

583
00:25:35.500 --> 00:25:37.500
I guess we were all tired and grouchy.
我猜我们当时都很累而且脾气暴躁。

584
00:25:37.700 --> 00:25:38.820
I guess so.
我也这么觉得。

585
00:25:39.600 --> 00:25:41.600
Lady, you said you had some questions.
女士，你之前说你有几个问题。

586
00:25:42.280 --> 00:25:42.920
I do.
我是有。

587
00:25:43.080 --> 00:25:44.240
I'm here to answer questions.
我就是来回答问题的。

588
00:25:44.460 --> 00:25:44.780
All right.
好的。

589
00:25:44.940 --> 00:25:49.920
So I know from other episodes where anytime we had to throw something, you don't get it
我从其他集里了解到，只要我们需要扔什么东西，你不可能一遍就过。

590
00:25:49.920 --> 00:25:50.760
on the first take.
但史蒂夫把起司球扔向你的那个镜头，你接住了。

591
00:25:51.440 --> 00:25:58.020
But that shot of Steve throwing the cheese puff ball at you, you caught it.
你把它咬住了。

592
00:25:58.160 --> 00:25:59.060
You chomped it.
你直接看向了镜头。

593
00:25:59.140 --> 00:26:00.100
You looked right to camera.
当时我就想，我的好姐妹，看看她。

594
00:26:00.220 --> 00:26:02.520
And I was like, my girl, look at her.
我太骄傲了。

595
00:26:02.700 --> 00:26:03.640
I was so proud.
我当时就想，天哪，简直是《双面女间谍》里的悉尼·布里斯托。

596
00:26:03.640 --> 00:26:06.720
I was like, okay, Sidney Bristow on alias.
你能做到吗？

597
00:26:06.920 --> 00:26:07.940
Can you do that?
珍娜，这就是你的高光时刻。

598
00:26:08.160 --> 00:26:09.700
Jenna, this is like your moment.
好吧。

599
00:26:10.240 --> 00:26:10.420
All right.
我要告诉你一件事。

600
00:26:10.420 --> 00:26:11.340
I'm going to tell you something.
我要告诉你一件事。

601
00:26:11.560 --> 00:26:11.840
Okay.
好吧。

602
00:26:12.120 --> 00:26:17.560
When I was in high school, I did not have a vibrant social life.
我上高中时，社交生活很不丰富。

603
00:26:18.260 --> 00:26:20.840
So you threw cheese balls at your face?
所以你把芝士球往自己脸 上扔？

604
00:26:21.020 --> 00:26:21.520
No.
没有。

605
00:26:21.780 --> 00:26:22.100
What?
什么？

606
00:26:22.260 --> 00:26:24.160
I watched a lot of movies.
我看了很多电影。

607
00:26:24.500 --> 00:26:24.740
Okay.
好吧。

608
00:26:25.080 --> 00:26:27.440
And when I watched the movies, I would eat popcorn.
看电影的时候，我会吃爆米花。

609
00:26:27.920 --> 00:26:32.680
And I started throwing the popcorn up in the air and catching it.
然后我开始把爆米花往空中扔，再用嘴接住。

610
00:26:32.800 --> 00:26:33.420
By yourself.
就你一个人。

611
00:26:33.660 --> 00:26:33.960
Yeah.
对。

612
00:26:34.180 --> 00:26:34.420
Okay.
好吧。

613
00:26:34.940 --> 00:26:36.920
Listen, it paid off later in my life.
听着，这在我后来的生活中帮了大忙。

614
00:26:36.920 --> 00:26:37.620
It sure did.
确实如此。

615
00:26:37.880 --> 00:26:38.380
It sure did.
确实如此。

616
00:26:38.380 --> 00:26:39.740
So don't feel sorry for me.
所以别同情我。

617
00:26:39.840 --> 00:26:40.840
I'm not feeling sorry.
我没有同情你。

618
00:26:40.840 --> 00:26:46.140
I also saw tons of great movies, and I have a great mind for the cinema.
我还看了无数好电影，我对电影有着极高的鉴赏力。

619
00:26:46.740 --> 00:26:47.260
Yes.
没错。

620
00:26:47.560 --> 00:26:51.560
So I am really good at catching food in my mouth.
所以我非常擅长用嘴接食物。

621
00:26:51.720 --> 00:26:52.220
I know.
我知道。

622
00:26:52.500 --> 00:26:56.140
Also, my sister and I would throw popcorn at each other.
另外，我和我姐会互相扔爆米花。

623
00:26:56.180 --> 00:26:56.280
Sure.
当然。

624
00:26:56.560 --> 00:26:56.720
Sure.
当然。

625
00:26:56.920 --> 00:27:01.560
So when I read this cold open, I was like, I'm going to nail this.
所以当我读到这个开场白时，心想，我绝对能搞定。

626
00:27:01.680 --> 00:27:01.740
Ding, ding, ding, ding, ding, ding, ding, ding.
叮，叮，叮，叮，叮，叮，叮，叮。

627
00:27:02.020 --> 00:27:05.100
And then I got really scared that they were going to want to CGI it.
然后我真的很害怕他们会想要用电脑特效做出来。

628
00:27:05.200 --> 00:27:06.580
Because you were like, guys, I got this.
因为你说，伙计们，我搞得定。

629
00:27:06.900 --> 00:27:08.000
It's not CGI.
这不是特效。

630
00:27:08.300 --> 00:27:08.680
No, I know.
不，我知道。

631
00:27:08.680 --> 00:27:10.680
I want everyone to know those are real cheese balls.
我想让每个人都知道那些都是真的芝士球。

632
00:27:11.580 --> 00:27:15.300
We had the best time shooting this.
我们拍摄时玩得可开心了。

633
00:27:15.500 --> 00:27:16.380
It looks like it.
看得出来。

634
00:27:16.380 --> 00:27:20.240
But I was just delighted by every moment of it.
但我对其中的每一个瞬间都感到欣喜若狂。

635
00:27:21.200 --> 00:27:23.440
Jenna, I'm great at catching food in my mouth as well.
珍娜，我也很擅长用嘴接食物。

636
00:27:24.280 --> 00:27:24.640
Oh.
哦。

637
00:27:24.960 --> 00:27:28.580
But just because I have good hand-eye coordination, because I'm a little bit of a sport-o.
但那只是因为我手眼协调能力好，因为我有点像个运动健将。

638
00:27:28.660 --> 00:27:30.620
Why have we never thrown food at one another?
为什么我们从来没互相扔过食物？

639
00:27:30.940 --> 00:27:32.000
What do we have in here?
这里面有什么？

640
00:27:32.080 --> 00:27:33.280
Can we throw something at each other?
我们能互相扔点东西吗？

641
00:27:33.280 --> 00:27:34.960
We have a little bit of granola bar.
我们有一点麦片能量棒。

642
00:27:35.160 --> 00:27:36.520
We have granola bar and alcohol.
我们有麦片能量棒和酒。

643
00:27:36.820 --> 00:27:37.740
That's not going to work.
那可不行。

644
00:27:39.920 --> 00:27:40.320
Well.
好吧。

645
00:27:40.500 --> 00:27:42.320
Next time, we're bringing popcorn.
下次我们带爆米花来。

646
00:27:43.500 --> 00:27:44.680
We can film that.
我们可以把那个拍下来。

647
00:27:44.880 --> 00:27:46.000
Sam's going to the kitchen.
山姆去厨房了。

648
00:27:46.420 --> 00:27:46.540
Oh, God.
哦，天哪。

649
00:27:46.560 --> 00:27:48.260
So maybe we'll get some food in a second.
所以我们一会儿可能会弄到点吃的。

650
00:27:49.320 --> 00:27:51.600
It did take us a whole afternoon to shoot this.
我们确实花了一整个下午才拍完这个。

651
00:27:51.600 --> 00:27:57.180
And the one that took the longest was the three-way, where-
花时间最长的是那个三人互投，就是——

652
00:27:57.180 --> 00:27:59.100
You just phrased that differently.
你只是换了个说法。

653
00:27:59.840 --> 00:28:01.780
I'm going to phrase it how I want to.
我想怎么说就怎么说。

654
00:28:01.900 --> 00:28:01.960
Okay.
好吧。

655
00:28:02.680 --> 00:28:03.200
Okay.
好吧。

656
00:28:07.460 --> 00:28:11.260
The one that took the longest was the three-way, as you were saying.
正如你刚才所说，花时间最长的是那个三人互投。

657
00:28:11.540 --> 00:28:11.980
Continue.
继续。

658
00:28:12.540 --> 00:28:14.080
You know, the one where-
你知道的，就是那个——

659
00:28:14.080 --> 00:28:14.960
Yes, I know.
对，我知道。

660
00:28:14.980 --> 00:28:18.380
Like, we're each throwing a cheese ball into a different person's mouth between the three
就是我们三个人，每个人把一个奶酪球

